comments.body:
@kinwin-ustc `cubemastercli tpl create-from-image` works — tested with `--cpu 1000/2000/4000`, all succeeded and cgroup CPU limits are written correctly (`200000 100000` for 2 cores).

The `MissingMemoryZones` error only occurs with `cubemastercli template create` (the JSON-file path), likely a Firecracker VM boot issue on AMD Strix Halo. Since `create-from-image` covers our use case, this is low priority for us.

One suggestion: the `--cpu` flag is well-documented as millicores in the CLI help, but CubeAPI's `cpu` field has no unit documentation. We initially passed `cpu: 2` thinking it meant 2 cores, but it's millicores (should be 2000). A note in the CubeAPI docs would help avoid confusion.
